WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:01.719
Okay.

00:00:01.719 --> 00:00:04.830
Let's talk about something I've been getting
a lot of questions about over the last couple

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:12.660
of weeks and the gist of the questions has
been, Hey David, why are you listed on Jordan

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.940
Peterson's new website?

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.940
Think spot.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.980
Why are you involved with Jordan Peterson?

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:18.980
Are you part of it?

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.029
Are you not part of it?

00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:22.830
I've not heard you mention it, but they list
you.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:23.830
So let's talk about it.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.900
I haven't been saying anything publicly because
there's been a lot going on behind the scenes,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.259
but I am ready to talk to you today about
it and I can report to you that I am no longer

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:36.650
in any way part of Jordan Peterson's website
think spot.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:40.330
But I do believe I owe you a full explanation
about everything that's gone down.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.310
And I'll tell you about it today.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:48.210
So months and months ago, in fact, it was
on July 2nd Jordan Peterson emailed me and

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.680
said, Hey David, I'm starting this thing.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.700
Think spot with some other people.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.710
Uh, we're bringing in a bunch of high profile
contributors.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:03.090
I thought of you, here's an introduction to
the people running it, talk to them.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.680
And I had no further contact with Jordan Peterson.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.180
I was put in touch with the folks at think
spot, all nice people.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.890
The idea was, Hey, we're bringing in a bunch
of big name contributors to our website.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:15.890
Thanks spot.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.260
We want you to be on there.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.340
You can do whatever you want.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.920
Of course, whatever content you already do
or want to start doing or whatever you can

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:23.920
do.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:29.420
So I of course have done a ton of criticisms
and take downs of Jordan Peterson and so when

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:35.190
I was approached I thought either a he and
they have no idea about that when they invited

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:39.570
me or they have an idea and they don't care
either way, it's not my problem.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:45.490
So I thought, what is my philosophy on the
show about appearing on different platforms?

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:50.520
My philosophy on this show has been when I
am invited to a new platform, if it's not

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.690
a lot more work for our team because we are
stretched pretty thin, I do it and we've launched

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:57.750
on a ton of different platforms over the last
few years.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.799
We launched on a platform called Steemit.

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:05.940
We launched our podcast on Pandora and Spotify
and radio.com we started put, putting our

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:13.160
clips on D tube and another one called library
LBR Y and three speak, and for lots of these

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:19.340
things there are people involved or founders
or corporations whose politics are not in

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:25.420
line with mine, but my view is my content
in more places without requiring a lot more

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.400
work for our team is good.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.650
I can increase my reach, I can get my content
in front of people.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.650
That's a good thing.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.810
That was my thought with the thing spot partnership.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:38.630
Now the launch of things spot got delayed
multiple times.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.500
I think at first it was going to be early
August, then late August, then I don't even

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.500
know when it launched.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.390
I think it was maybe in October, but eventually
it launched and when things bought launched,

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.250
it launched with really no other contributors
that I think were well aligned with the David

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.830
Pakman show.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:57.790
Engagement was very low and I'll be honest,
my ability to engage with the platform is

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:03.680
also low because we're very busy at the end
of the day and then I saw this may actually

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.310
be an acutely bad platform for us to be on.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:12.140
It's not like some of these others, uh, some
of these other platforms where there are tons

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:15.230
of contributors and I'm there putting up my
stuff.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:18.379
It was like eight contributors that were being
promoted.

00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:22.600
One of those contributors is Jordan Peterson's
daughter whose content was being sold for

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.920
even more than mine when I, which I found
sort of jarring and in Congress I think our

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.510
content is mostly around eating like a meat
only diet or something like that.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.310
So long story short, I respectfully told them,
I don't think this is the right platform for

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.310
me.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:39.420
The way it's shaken out, there's no real cadre
of other contributors that are kind of doing

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.770
what we're doing at the level we're doing
it in our space.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:43.670
I don't think it's helping me.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:48.680
They also said we're going to be transitioning
from a subscription model to more of a micro

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.099
payments model.

00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:54.050
That makes it even less suited for us because
we're already on a bunch of those and I don't

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:57.569
want to spread our micropayment platforms
too thin.

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:01.770
So as far as I've been told you can no longer
subscribe to me on things spot.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:06.830
They are in the process of removing my content
altogether and this is sort of more in line

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:11.280
with what's going to be our 2020 strategy,
which is now I think we are at a point where

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.470
I'm not looking to get on more and more and
more platforms and spread ourselves really

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:16.470
thin.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.699
I'm reeling in the platforms that we're on.

00:04:18.699 --> 00:04:21.810
We're going to focus on a few platforms that
are working well for us, so we're going to

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:22.940
try to grow YouTube.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.700
We're going to try to grow Facebook and Instagram
video.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.310
We're going to grow the podcast.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.419
That will be the focus.

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:33.699
Now I've got a couple of questions on Twitter
saying, David, are you going to return the

00:04:33.699 --> 00:04:35.190
money?

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.660
The first answer is we never got any money.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.720
I mean we didn't get any money for signing
up and we were getting a cut of subscriptions

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.480
for people signed up.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:43.580
I never got any money.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.630
I don't know what the payment schedule is
supposed to be.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.490
There was no money to return.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.050
But beyond that, I don't know why I would
return money.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.380
Like if people don't like this platform, me
keeping money gives them less money.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.860
You think you would want me to do that?

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:00.570
But in any case, there is no money for people
got paid subscriptions and none of the money

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.729
ever came to me.

00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:04.750
Uh, and I don't predict that it ever will.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:05.970
So that's that.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:10.530
And no, I also am not joining Dave Rubin's
new platform either.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.830
I don't know much about that one, but I can
assure you I am not involved.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:47.240
And that is the Thor

00:05:47.240 --> 00:07:15.510
is 
the story with think spot.

